※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4486

※ It takes no arguments, because it is not a function: it is written around the
※ one expression whose operators are to wrap.  Written around two there is no
※ such expression, and what the second one was meant to be is anyone's guess.

let a: u8 = 200u8
let b: u8 = 100u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕wrap(a, b)
